\section{Conventions that define the model}{

Column order of \code{Z}: \code{column = (a - 1) * q + level}, level fastest.
Order of \code{theta}: for each term the \code{Sigma} parameters then the between-level
parameters, terms in declaration order, then the residual, then each \code{dsum}
section. \code{theta} is a log standard deviation for a variance (\verb{var = exp(2 theta)}) and the floor is \code{-12} by default. Row order in a separable product:
\code{level = (row - 1) * n_col + col}. Changing any of these on one side only
yields a different model with no error.
}

\section{Reading a fit}{

Read \code{newton_decrement} (the log-likelihood still available under the local
quadratic model, comparable to 3.84 for a one-degree-of-freedom LRT) rather
than \code{max_grad}, which is several units at verified optima. \code{logLik}
includes \verb{(n - p)/2 log(2 pi)} like lme4; asreml omits it, use
\code{logLik_asreml} to compare. \code{composantes_degenerees} names the terms with a
parameter at the floor: those are unidentified, not estimated at zero.
}

